 No registered estimate or decision changed.”

 The response’s two carried-over round-2 edits are present. In particular, “which is within search error” now
 appears in the abstract. Its presence verifies the response’s account; it does not make that claim scientifically
 justified.



 4. Reset follow-up

 (a) Plan fidelity
 The central analysis implements the stated estimands and rules. Verification has several distinct scopes:

  Plan section                   Finding


  1. Previously observed         The supplied headline B3, R3, and C∗ records reproduce the motivating contrasts. The plan’s B2 headline
  evidence                       row is not checkable from this package because the corresponding B2 records are absent. The fact that
                                 these outcomes were already known is disclosed.


  2. Estimand                    Correct. I is the paired difference between separately training-selected D2+H3 and D2 winners against an
                                 unchanged reference. All supplied fresh rule-market pairs have matching seed arrays, normalizers, reference
                                 hashes, and per-seed reference profits across families and search versions. It is not the optimal option value
                                 of replacement.


  4. Diagnostics                 Fresh-market fixed-policy switch-off and reverse-switch calculations are implemented and aggregate
                                 correctly; every base D2 winner has zero recorded resets. The supplied diagnostic file contains the fresh
                                 cells, but not the additional headline diagnostic evaluations specified by the complete plan. Full
                                 seven-market diagnostic coverage is therefore not checkable here. C∗’s switch effects are in R.switches but
                                 omitted from the paper’s switch-effect sentence.


  5. Analysis                    Correct: 9,999 paired percentile-bootstrap resamples; one resampled index vector shared across rules and
                                 families within each market; independent resampling across markets; equal market weights; the ratio
                                 recalculated within resamples; the 0.05 denominator-floor check applied separately to pooled and
                                 leave-one-out analyses; no clipping of S. Frozen and doubled results and attack/reference changes are
                                 retained.


  6. Expectations                Correct: the B3 interaction on every market is “met”; the C∗ interaction is “not established
                                 (search-sensitive)”; pooled S > 0.5 is “met.” The labels compare both prescribed versions and are
                                 descriptive, as the plan requires.


 The driver visibly preserves the original stage functions while introducing the documented manifest,
 doubling-eligibility, and freeze exceptions. The supplied records support the pairing contract. I cannot
 independently establish the full runner behavior without its imported simulator and stage code.

 The later review_r3 block is numerically correct and explicitly labelled “added after external review r3 (Fable
 5.2); exploratory.” Its market-level intervals, sign counts, flag summary, and leave-one-out range reproduce.
 Its name nesting_failures and associated interpretation should change for the reasons below. Without an
 earlier reset.json snapshot or repository history, I can verify current calculations, not independently
 authenticate the response’s historical assertion that all earlier fields were unchanged.

 The ledger now records a plan commit at 05:52 UTC, pod launch at 13:43, analysis-code commit at 16:47:33,
 and first analysis run at 16:48:02, on its stated follow-up date. It explicitly acknowledges that the records were
 already on disk before the analysis-code commit. These times come from operations-ledger.md, “Reset
 follow-up.” The gate reports bit identity, and its file hash matches the ledger’s prefix; I did not reproduce that
 execution.


